## 2026-05-14 — UID validator caught a 5-word skill name

**Cart / Phase:** Bootyful Demake (chunked run), UID assignment

**What happened:** During UID assignment, the validator flagged `match_world_to_screen_coords` as having 5 words instead of 4 (`match` / `world` / `to` / `screen` / `coords`).

**Resolution:** Renamed to `match_world_screen_coords` (dropped "to"). Meaning preserved, format compliant with the 4-word rule.

**Lesson:** Programmatic validation catches naming drift that visual review misses. The 4-word rule is enforced at UID-assignment time, not at extraction time. Reviewers will not catch every off-by-one; tooling will.

